commit_report_chapter_batch({'chapters': [{'chapter_id': 1, 'bundle_token': 
'b1-0c96ed4e', 'content': 'The **Ring of Nestor** is a Mycenaean gold signet 
ring dating to the 16th–15th century BC and now kept in the National 
Archaeological Museum in Athens, within the Collection of Prehistoric 
Antiquities (inv. no. P 6209).[3] The ring forms part of the so‑called Tiryns 
Hoard, a group of gold rings and bead seals reportedly discovered in 1915 in a 
rock‑cut chamber tomb near Thisbê in Boeotia, and later associated with the 
site of Tiryns in the Argolid.[2][3] Its oval bezel, about 2 × 3.4 cm in size 
